message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Lares"
    given-names: "Ezequiel"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
title: "Cancer Research: Cross-Literature Analysis and Ferroptosis Simulation"
type: software
version: "2026-04"
date-released: "2026-04-23"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/ELares/cancer_research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ELares/cancer_research"
abstract: >
  Open-source cancer research combining a census of the indexed cancer
  literature -- 5,187,265 articles, being 4,403,994 with MeSH indexing
  and 783,271 recovered by text match, carrying 10,509,470 typed entity
  relations -- with Monte Carlo biochemical simulations of ferroptosis
  sensitivity across cell phenotypes, drug combinations, and tumor
  microenvironment features. Claims are measured over articles the
  project did not select, using expert-assigned MeSH descriptors and
  NLM publication types rather than the project's own retrieval.
  Includes a reusable Rust simulation engine (ferroptosis-core) with
  Python bindings, a news source authentication pipeline, and a
  ~115-page book-format manuscript.
keywords:
  - cancer research
  - ferroptosis
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - cross-literature analysis
  - drug-tolerant persister cells
  - tumor microenvironment
  - sonodynamic therapy
  - open science
